{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q423323","formula":"H₂N₂","hill":"H2N2","elements":["H","N"],"composition":{"H":2.0,"N":2.0},"names":{"en":"Diazene","ru":"Диимид"},"descriptions":{"en":"Diimide, also called diazene or diimine, is a compound having the formula HN=NH. It exists as two geometric isomers, E (trans) and Z (cis). The term diazene is more common for organic derivatives of diimide. Thus, azobenzene is an example of an organic diazene.","ru":"Диимид (также диазен или диимин) — химическое соединение с формулой N2H2. Существует в виде двух геометрических изомеров: E (транс) и Z (цис). Термин «диазен» чаще применяется к органическим производным диимида; так, азобензол является примером органического диазена."},"fame":21,"pubchemCid":123195,"mass":30.03,"charge":0,"smiles":"N=N","inchikey":"RAABOESOVLLHRU-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"diazene","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"123195","atoms":4,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.622,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.622,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":0.998,"y":0.945,"z":-0.135,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.998,"y":-0.945,"z":0.135,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,1,2],[0,2,1],[1,3,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q423323","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diimide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%94%D0%B8%D0%B8%D0%BC%D0%B8%D0%B4","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"properties","name":"PubChem","url":"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/123195","license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},{"role":"structure","name":"PubChem 3D","url":"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/123195#section=3D-Conformer","license":"PubChem (NIH